 "result_text": "I fixed this in `nose2/session.py`. `nose2 -c tox.ini --junit-xml` should no longer fail with \"Unrecognized arguments\". I haven't run it or the test suite.\n\n**Cause:** `loadConfigFiles` only read files ending in `.cfg`. It read `.toml` files only if the name ended in `pyproject.toml`. Anything else, such as `tox.ini`, was silently skipped. Your `[unittest] plugins` list was never loaded, so `--junit-xml` didn't exist.\n\n**Fix:** any filename ending in `.toml` is now parsed as TOML, and every other filename is read as an ini-style file. Previously only a file named `pyproject.toml` was treated as TOML. So a differently named `.toml` file passed with `-c` is now read as TOML instead of being skipped.",
